    "summary": "A woman&#039;s skirt wrap, known as a &#039;katrinca&#039;. Rectangular in shape, with a solid black centre [66 cm wide] bordered by predominantly brown panels.  Twill woven [2/2 twill] from wool, hand woven, with selvedges worn at the waist and hem.  The two bordering panels [35.5 cm approx] have alternating brown wool and multicoloured wool and cotton stripes (woven as bands): pink, green, yellow, blue woollen thread and pale pink silk thread.  The warp ends are turned and hemmed. Some wear in the black centre field, including two large holes.",
